content.thinking:
Now I can see the issue! The `resolveGatewayStartupPluginIds` function determines which plugins are loaded at startup. Looking at the filter logic:

```javascript
.filter((plugin) => {
  if (plugin.channels.some((channelId) => configuredChannelIds.has(channelId))) {
    return true;
  }
  if (plugin.channels.length > 0) {
    return false;
  }
  ...
})
```

The issue is that if a plugin has channels (like Discord has `channels: ["discord"]`), but `configuredChannelIds` doesn't contain "discord", then the plugin is filtered out! It returns `false` at the `if (plugin.channels.length > 0) { return false; }` check.


So Discord gets excluded because the `openclaw doctor` migration likely transformed the config structure—instead of having `"channels": { "discord": { "accounts": [...] } }`, it probably restructured it to something like `"channels": { "discord-bot": ... }` that doesn't match the original channel ID. I need to check what `listPotentialConfiguredChannelIds` actually returns and trace through the diff between those two versions to understand how the config changed.

